WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.547
Hi, I'm Freesia!

00:00:02.547 --> 00:00:07.158
Modular's handbook prices an LLM's memory and speed with simple formulas.

00:00:09.183 --> 00:00:10.567
Every formula is right.

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:15.412
What matters is the input: a KV cache counts cached heads, not attention heads.

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:21.038
Here's one token's cache, for Llama 3 8B.

00:00:21.458 --> 00:00:23.738
Thirty-two layers, each with its own cache.

00:00:25.282 --> 00:00:30.208
Eight KV heads, not thirty-two attention heads: four query heads share each cached head.

00:00:30.628 --> 00:00:34.665
Head dimension one twenty-eight, two bytes each: about a hundred and thirty-one

00:00:34.665 --> 00:00:36.010
thousand bytes a token.

00:00:37.708 --> 00:00:41.646
Qwen3-Next has forty-eight layers; only every fourth keeps a KV cache.

00:00:41.646 --> 00:00:43.794
The rest hold a fixed state.

00:00:44.214 --> 00:00:48.299
In those twelve, sixteen query heads share two cached heads: eight times

00:00:48.299 --> 00:00:50.001
smaller, then four times again.

00:00:50.421 --> 00:00:54.742
With attention heads, the handbook's calculator says a hundred and ninety-two gigabytes.

00:00:54.742 --> 00:00:56.542
The real cache is six.

00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:03.179
A draft model reads the context and guesses three tokens ahead: nice, today, outside.

00:01:03.599 --> 00:01:06.853
The target checks all three in one pass, keeping the longest

00:01:06.853 --> 00:01:08.037
prefix it agrees with.

00:01:08.457 --> 00:01:12.277
It keeps nice and today, rejects outside, and adds its own: for.

00:01:12.277 --> 00:01:13.550
Three tokens, one pass.

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:16.953
Servers log accepted over proposed: two thirds.

00:01:16.953 --> 00:01:22.066
Leviathan's formula wants something else: the chance each reached position is accepted.

00:01:23.842 --> 00:01:26.570
In the handbook's own drawing: two ticks, and a cross.

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:30.989
Everything after the first rejection is discarded, so the logged rate falls

00:01:30.989 --> 00:01:32.322
as you draft further.

00:01:33.758 --> 00:01:38.957
Fed that logged rate, the formula runs fifty-five percent low at seven drafted tokens.

00:01:42.933 --> 00:01:45.649
A formula is only as right as its input.

00:01:45.649 --> 00:01:48.969
Price the cache from KV heads, cached layers and cache type.

00:01:51.525 --> 00:01:55.111
To recap: count KV heads and cached layers, and know which

00:01:55.111 --> 00:01:56.415
acceptance rate you have.

00:01:56.835 --> 00:01:59.021
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:59.021 --> 00:01:59.645
I'm Freesia.

00:01:59.645 --> 00:01:59.957
Bye!
